DESCRIPTION:First Stage Series:\n\nThe First Stage Series at the University
  of North Texas offers senior students a distinctive opportunity to self-d
 irect a theatrical production on campus. To participate\, students must su
 bmit a proposal to a committee of faculty and staff and receive approval. 
 These productions are entirely student-driven\, encompassing all aspects f
 rom casting and rehearsals to the final direction of the show.\n\nAbout An
 tigone Now:\n\nSet against the ruins of a city still reeling from war\, th
 is modern retelling follows the fiercely determined Antigone as she stands
  in defiance of her uncle’s decree to honor her fallen brother. Her act 
 of resistance sparks a powerful conflict between personal loyalty and poli
 tical authority. With vivid contemporary language and emotional intensity\
 , this adaptation reexamines an ancient myth\, highlighting the enduring s
 truggles of family\, duty\, and moral courage in a fractured world.\n\n   
             Written by: Melissa Cooper\n               Director: Sophia Ag
 uirre\n               Run Time: 60 Minutes\n\nTheatre Information:\n\nWe a
 re thrilled to invite you to a captivating live performance in the Black B
 ox Theatre (RTFP 127)\, located in the Radio\, TV\, Film\, and Performing 
 Arts Building at 1179 Union Circle\, Denton\, Texas\, 76201. For maps\, di
 rections\, and parking information\, please visit our website here.\n\nTo 
 ensure a smooth and enjoyable experience\, we kindly ask that you arrive 2
 0-30 minutes before your selected show time. Our performance will begin pr
 omptly\, and we want to make sure you don't miss a moment of the magic. Pl
 ease note that late seating is not permitted. For the comfort and enjoymen
 t of all our guests\, no food or drink is allowed in the performance space
 s. Additionally\, recording or videography of any kind is strictly prohibi
 ted once the performance begins. The Box Office does not offer refunds or 
 exchanges.\n\nThis show has general admission seating. Seating will be fir
 st come\, first served\, with house doors opening at 7:00PM and doors clos
 ing promptly at 7:30PM. If you arrive after the doors have closed\, you wi
 ll not be able to enter the show.\n\nThank you for supporting the UNT Danc
 e and Theatre Department. We can't wait to welcome you and share this spec
 ial experience with you. See you soon!
